        list1.printList();
        System.out.println("List 2:");
        list2.printList();

        LinkedList sumList = list1.addLists(list2);
        System.out.println("Sum of lists:");
        sumList.printList();
    }
}
```

This program creates two linked lists (list1 and list2) and adds them using the `addLists()` method. The `addToList()` method is used to add nodes to the linked lists, and the `printList()` method is used to print the contents of the linked lists. The `addLists()` method takes another LinkedList as an argument and returns the sum of the two linked lists as a new LinkedList.

