 Here's a Java program that calculates the area of a triangle using Heron's formula. Heron's formula is used when you have the lengths of all three sides of a triangle.

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class TriangleArea {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter the length of side A: ");
        double sideA = scanner.nextDouble();

        System.out.print("Enter the length of side B: ");
        double sideB = scanner.nextDouble();

        System.out.print("Enter the length of side C: ");
        double sideC = scanner.nextDouble();

        double s = (sideA + sideB + sideC) / 2.0; // semi-perimeter
        double area = Math.sqrt(s * (s - sideA) * (s - sideB) * (s - sideC));

        System.out.printf("The area of the triangle is: %.2f%n", area);
    }
}
```

