public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ArrayList<String> fruits = new ArrayList<>();
        fruits.add("Apple");
        fruits.add("Banana");
        fruits.add("Orange");

        Iterator<String> iterator = fruits.iterator();
        while (iterator.hasNext()) {
            String fruit = iterator.next();
            System.out.println(fruit);
        }
    }
}
```

In this example, we create an ArrayList of strings, get an Iterator for the list, and iterate through the elements using a while loop. The `hasNext()` method checks if there are more elements to iterate, and the `next()` method retrieves the next element. The output of this program will be:

