 To create a Java program that finds the 10 numbers closest to a given number, you can use the Absolute Difference method. Here's a simple implementation:

```java
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.stream.IntStream;

public class ClosestNumbers {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int givenNumber = 50;
        int limit = 100;
        List<Integer> numbers = IntStream.rangeClosed(1, limit)
                .boxed()
                .toList();

        numbers.sort( (a, b) -> Math.abs(a - givenNumber) - Math.abs(b - givenNumber) );

        System.out.println("The 10 numbers closest to " + givenNumber + " are:");
        for (int i = 0; i < 10 && i < numbers.size(); i++) {
            System.out.print(numbers.get(i) + " ");
        }
    }
}
```

This program generates a list of numbers from 1 to the given limit (100 by default), sorts them based on the absolute difference from the given number, and then prints the first 10 numbers. You can change the `givenNumber` and `limit` variables to find the closest numbers for different values.

