MongoDB uses a NoSQL (non-relational) database model, which allows for more flexible and dynamic schema design compared to traditional relational databases. This means that the structure of a collection (a group of documents) in MongoDB can evolve over time, as new fields can be added to individual documents without affecting the entire collection.

